  "summary": "Malicious code in bnpl-blocks-mobile-bnpl-link-group (npm)",
  "details": "On require, the package downloads a platform-specific second-stage binary over HTTPS from Cloudflare Workers hosts (oob-worker[.]cf101-adf[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf102-baf[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf103-070[.]workers[.]dev) at paths /pkg/package, /pkg/package-arm64, /pkg/loader_mac, or /pkg/package.exe depending on OS/arch. If HTTPS fails it retrieves the payload via DNS TXT records chunked from the wel1[.]ru domain family (c[.]sdk[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru). The downloaded binary is written to /var/tmp/.cache_\u0026lt;hex\u0026gt; (or dotnet_diag_\u0026lt;hex\u0026gt;.exe under %TEMP% on Windows), chmod 755, and executed detached via /bin/sh or cmd.exe /c start /b, so it runs in the background and outlives the parent process.",
